# PB-CORE-006 — Enumeration Theorem

## Theorem

Let X be an n-element finite set.

For each total map

    T : X -> X,

let

    Stab(T)
      =
    {E in Eq(X) : T*E = E}.

Then the total number of pullback-fixed equivalence relations over
all labeled maps T : X -> X is

    A_n
      =
    n!
    sum_{k=1}^n
      k p(k) n^(n-k-1)
      /
      (n-k)!,

where p(k) is the number of integer partitions of k.

Equivalently,

    A_n
      =
    sum_{T:X->X} |Stab(T)|.

---

## Proof architecture

1. Every finite T has a periodic core P.

2. T|P is a permutation.

3. Pullback-fixed equivalences of T are in bijection with invariant
   equivalences of T|P.

4. If |P|=k, summing over all permutations of P gives

       k! p(k).

5. A fixed k-element core can receive

       k n^(n-k-1)

   rooted forests from the remaining n-k labeled vertices.

6. Choose the core in

       binomial(n,k)

   ways.

7. Sum over k.

This yields

    A_n
      =
    sum_k
      binomial(n,k)
      k n^(n-k-1)
      k!p(k),

which simplifies to the stated formula.

---

## Evidence

[P] mathematical derivation.

[V] exhaustive all-map check for n <= 7.

[V] independent permutation formula checks.

[PV] exact values n <= 12 obtained from the theorem.

---

## Novelty boundary

No claim is made that the underlying cycle congruence theory is new.

The relevant classical literature includes Berman's work on unary
algebra congruence lattices, subsequent work on monounary algebras,
and G-set congruence theory.

The AQARION-specific contribution is the synthesis around the
pullback-fixed relation T*E=E and the explicit finite dynamical
core/extension classification, together with executable verification
and provenance.

A separate literature search is still required before making a
priority claim for the enumeration formula itself.
